*  fizzbuzz.sno -- one to a hundred, Fizz for three, Buzz for five.
*  Part of github.com/mdhender/sil. BSD 2-Clause; see LICENSE.
*
*  Written on the failure of a statement rather than on branches: an
*  assignment whose right side contains a predicate that fails does
*  not happen, so LINE keeps what it had. REMDR, concatenation and a
*  hundred turns of the loop.
        N = 0
LOOP    N = LT(N,100) N + 1            :F(END)
        LINE =
        LINE = EQ(REMDR(N,3),0) 'Fizz'
        LINE = EQ(REMDR(N,5),0) LINE 'Buzz'
        LINE = IDENT(LINE) N
        OUTPUT = LINE                  :(LOOP)
END
